d from <italic>p</italic>-isopropylbenzaldehyde thiosemicarbazone with cytotoxicity against cisplatin resistant tumor cell lines</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Inorganic Biochemistry</italic></source><year>1998</year><volume>69</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>275</fpage><lpage>281</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9654751</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vila</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Pereira</surname><given-names>MaT</given-names></name><name><surname>Ortigueira</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Formation, characterization, and structural studies of novel thiosemicarbazone palladium(II) complexes. Crystal structures of [{Pd[C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>4</sub>C(ET) = NN = C(S)NH<sub>2</sub>]}<sub>4</sub>], [Pd{C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>4</sub>C(ET) = NN = C(S)NH<sub>2</sub>}(PMePh<sub>2</sub>)] and [{Pd[C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>4</sub>C(ET) = NN = C(S)NH<sub>2</sub>]}<sub>2</sub>(<italic>&#x003bc;</italic>-Ph<sub>2</sub>PCH<sub>2</sub>PPh<sub>2</sub>)]</article-title><source><italic>Journal of the Chemical Society, Dalton Transactions</italic></source><year>1999</year><issue>23</issue><fpage>4193</fpage><lpage>4201</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Salyn</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name><name><surname>Zumadilov</surname><given-names>NK</given-names></name><name><surname>Nefedov</surname><given-names>VI</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>ESCA Investigations on Heavy Metal Chelates of Substituted N-acyl-thio- and &#x02013;selenoureas</article-title><source><italic>Zeitschrift f&#x000fc;r Anorganische  und Allgemeine Chemie</italic></source><year>1977</year><volume>432</volume><fpage>p. 275</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Herzschuh</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Birner</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Beyer</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Dietze</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoyer</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mass Spectrometric Fragmentation of N-Benzoyl(thio)benzamides, N-Benzoyl(thio, seleno)ureas, and their Ni(II)- and Cu(II)-1:2-chelates</article-title><source><italic>Zeitschrift f&#x000fc;r Anorganische und Allgemeine Chemie</italic></source><year>1980</year><volume>464</volume><fpage>p. 159</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hern&#x000e1;ndez</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Spodine</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Hallmeier</surname><given-names>K-H</given-names></name><name><surname>Richter</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Schr&#x000f6;der</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Beyer</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Platinum(II) Mixed Ligand Complexes with Thiourea Derivatives, Dimethyl Sulphoxide and Chloride: Syntheses, Molecular Structures, and ESCA Data</article-title><source><italic>Zeitschrift f&#x000fc;r Anorganische und Allgemeine Chemie</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>629</volume><issue>14</issue><fpage>p. 259</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hern&#x000e1;ndez</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Spodine</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Mu&#x000f1;oz</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Synthesis, characterization and antitumor activity of <italic>cis</italic>-bis(acylthioureato) platinum(II) complexes, <italic>cis</italic>-PtL<sub>2</sub>[HL<sup>1</sup>=N,N-diphenyl-<italic>N</italic>&#x02032;-benzoylthiourea or HL<sup>2</sup> = N,N-diphenyl-<italic>N</italic>&#x02032;-(p-nitrobenzoyl)thiourea]</article-title><source><italic>Bioinorganic Chemistry and Applications</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>1</volume><issue>3-4</issue><fpage>271</fpage><lpage>284</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hern&#x000e1;ndez</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Spodine</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Beyer</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Synthesis, characterization and antitumor activity of copper(II) complexes, [CuL<sub>2</sub>] [HL<sup>1&#x02212;3</sup>=N,N-diethyl-N&#x02032;-(R-benzoyl)thiourea (R=H, o-Cl and p-NO<sub>2</sub>)]</article-title><source><italic>Bioinorganic Chemistry and Applications</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>3</volume><issue>3-4</issue><fpage>299</fpage><lpage>316</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lobana</surname><given-names>TS</given-names></name><name><surname>S&#x000e1;nchez</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Casas</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Symmetrisation, isomerism and structural studies on novel phenylmercury(II) thiosemicarbazonates: correlation of the energy barrier to rotation of the amino group with the bonding parameters of the thioamide group</article-title><source><italic>Journal of the Chemical Society, Dalton Transactions</italic></source><year>1997</year><issue>22</issue><fpage>4289</fpage><lpage>4300</lp