ter" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.07</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Prostate carcinoma (PC-3)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">10.20</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.56</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">7.36</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.08</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Chronic myelogenous leukemia (K562)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6.15</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.45</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.04</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.08</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>						<sup>(a)</sup>Cl<sub>50</sub> corresponds to the concentrationrequired to inhibit a 50% of the cell growth when the cells are exposed to thecompounds during 48 hours. Each value is the average of two independentexperiments.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>